<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto Braun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto Braun was a German Social Democratic politician who was minister-president of the Free State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> almost continuously from 1920 to 1932. His coalition with the Centre and liberals made Prussia a bulwark of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> until Chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-von-papen">Franz von Papen</a> deposed it in July 1932. He went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-braun.jpg" alt="Otto Braun" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Free State of Prussia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_Braun_1932_(Landtag)_Edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
